The three OntoOps services under services/ (CQ generation, ontoagent and
ontorouter) are part of this work and are licensed under the same terms.

Third-party components the service images install at build time (not
redistributed in this repository; versions are fixed by each service's
uv.lock):

- psycopg, psycopg-binary, psycopg-pool (LGPL-3.0), used unmodified as
  dynamically loaded libraries by all three services.
- owlready2 (LGPL-3.0-or-later), used by ontoagent. Its wheel bundles the
  HermiT reasoner (LGPL), which ontoagent calls for consistency checks, and
  the Pellet reasoner with its dependencies (Pellet: AGPL-3.0), which
  ontoagent never invokes; the jars are present in the image only because
  they ship inside the owlready2 wheel.
- opendataloader-pdf (Apache-2.0), used by CQ generation. It bundles a Java
  command-line jar with its own third-party notices, kept in the installed
  package under opendataloader_pdf/THIRD_PARTY/.
- OpenJDK (GPL-2.0 with the Classpath Exception), the Java runtime installed
  from Debian in the CQ generation and ontoagent images to run the two jars
  above.
- Other Python dependencies under permissive licences (MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0),
  among them FastAPI, pydantic, LangChain, the OpenAI and Langfuse clients,
  rdflib, falkordb, numpy and rapidfuzz.

The experiments run these services on a Docker Compose stack that pulls
third-party images carrying their own licences, also not redistributed here:
PostgreSQL with pgvector (PostgreSQL License), FalkorDB (Server Side Public
License v1; used as a local store, never offered as a service), and Hugging
Face text-embeddings-inference (Apache-2.0). The language models are served
outside the stack; their weights are not distributed here.
